{"cluster_id": "C-3162", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B010-077"], "canonical_claim": "A point ref lookup selects at most one base run using non-overlapping key bounds; a cold run normally requires `HEAD`, a footer range `GET`, and an indexed-block range `GET`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#gc-owned-fold-format"]}
