{"cluster_id": "C-3167", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B012-047"], "canonical_claim": "Read-only consumers such as fsck and inspect use the shared `replay` implementation with restart-on-vanish; fsck compares cache replay bytes with published snapshot bytes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L377-L385"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3168", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B013-035"], "canonical_claim": "Directory shape dispatch must preserve the fixed order `shadow \u2192 atomic-shard \u2192 table-uuid \u2192 part \u2192 subdir \u2192 generic`, and both `existsDirectory` and `listDirectory` must consume one shared routing table.", "issue_ids": ["A-D8", "A\u00a713.2#7"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L1973-L2116", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L165-L168"]}
