{"cluster_id": "C-3176", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B021-069"], "canonical_claim": "The recovery retry loop runs inside the existing `recovery_in_progress` single-flight guard, catches only `Exception` with `ErrorCodes::NETWORK_ERROR`, and immediately rethrows `CORRUPTED_DATA`, decode errors, `LOGICAL_ERROR`, and the `kRefRecoveryMaxRestarts` brake.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader.md#L43-L48"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3177", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B021-071"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery retry backoff is capped exponential, calculated as `min(recovery_retry_max_backoff_ms, recovery_retry_initial_backoff_ms << retry_num)`, and the retry loop re-runs recovery from a fresh `LIST`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader.md#L260-L300", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader.md#L43-L48"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3178", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B021-073"], "canonical_claim": "If a failed recovery attempt assigned `rt.state` or `rt.cleanup_markers`, the next retry replays and reassigns them before `rt.recovered` is set, overwriting the partial attempt cleanly.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader.md#L43-L48"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3179", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B022-015"], "canonical_claim": "A lazily loaded CAS table does not start replication queues or merges until its first access.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-20-cas-table-load-stuck-asyncloader-design.md#layer-2"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3180", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B023-054"], "canonical_claim": "Before a pre-terminal or read-only enumeration answers empty at a `TableDir` or `DetachedContainer` root, it must perform one authoritative uncached `probeSentinel(_pool_meta)`; absence yields a typed throw rather than an empty result.", "issue_ids": ["T9"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lease-loss-throw-and-stop-verbs-design.md#L39-L43"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3181", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B026-034", "B026-041"], "canonical_claim": "A diagnostic CAS reader that does not claim ownership must not schedule GC or mint writer state, and read-only enforcement should be below facade checks at the CAS `Backend` layer.; The recommended reader contract is observe-only by process role: a CA disk opened by a non-`SERVER` application never claims the mount, mints writer state, or schedules GC, while writable tool access requires an explicit opt-in.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-tool-read-without-ownership-design.md#recommendation"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3182", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B026-036"], "canonical_claim": "A mounted `Pool` caches `RefTableState` and does not re-recover it, while `CasFsck.cpp` deliberately uses a fresh `recoverRefTable`; a non-claiming read can therefore be less stale on the ref lane than a mounted read.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-tool-read-without-ownership-design.md#what-the-claim-protects"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3183", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B026-037"], "canonical_claim": "A non-claiming read-only pool has an unarmed local write fence, so the current read-only guarantee depends on seven `checkNotReadOnly` facade checks and on not starting the GC scheduler; the CAS `Backend` interface itself has no read-only concept.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-tool-read-without-ownership-design.md#read-only-gaps"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3184", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B027-046", "B027-055", "B037-057", "B045-049", "B050-031"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery never infers committed history from LIST or surviving objects; it exact-reads `_ckpt`, replays the finite arithmetic range through `committed_through`, and treats a missing required key at or below that frontier as corruption.; Read-only and writer recovery perform no stream LIST for completeness: recovery starts from the exact checkpoint and replays exact keys arithmetically to the committed frontier; LIST is only GC/janitor discovery.; Recovery must treat paginated `LIST` as a zero-trust hint rather than truth and must walk the ref-log tail by arithmetic point reads.; Cold ref-table recovery reads the namespace checkpoint through `readCkpt` and `backend.get(layout.refCkptKey(life))`; it does not recover by listing the namespace stream prefix.; After Task 5b, `LIST(cas/ns/stream/)` may provide snapshot candidates, diagnostics, performance hints, or leak-only cleanup nominations, but it may not be a correctness authority.", "issue_ids": ["T5b"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1a-report.md#L51-L77", ".superpowers/sdd/task-5b-list-audit.md#L7-L10", "docs/superpowers/models/CaRefTableSnapshotLogCore_RESULTS.md#L189-L197", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#recovery"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3185", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B027-050"], "canonical_claim": "Life-owned readers carry `NamespaceLifeId{namespace, incarnation}` and a stale reader receives stale-or-`NotFound`; all ref and namespace-file prefix/key/cache helpers require the typed life id, while namespace-only overloads are deleted.", "issue_ids": ["r9-3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3186", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B027-133"], "canonical_claim": "Recovery's arithmetic tail exact-reads every successor key, including ids omitted by the hint; a 404 below a durable higher same-epoch id causes bounded restart and eventual `CORRUPTED_DATA`, never partial replay.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-a-streams.md#task-6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3187", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B028-007", "B032-005", "B032-031", "B032-050", "B045-050", "B045-051"], "canonical_claim": "Namespace-file incarnation qualification must preserve the existing direct-object operation profile: no catalog request per file operation, no ref-log append, no blob upload, no folder-manifest rewrite, and unchanged backend request counts.; Steady-state namespace-file operations do not issue hot-path requests for catalog, ref-blob, manifest, or blob keys. Additionally, `CasNamespaceFileDiskProfile.SteadyStateFileOperationsTouchNoCatalogRefBlobOrManifestKey` is the existing disk-level proof for zero hot-path catalog/ref/blob/manifest requests, but its claim should be rechecked if a later held-life test finds a residual request on listing. Additionally, `CasNamespaceFileDiskProfile.SteadyStateFileOperationsTouchNoCatalogRefBlobOrManifestKey` records zero accesses to `layout.refCatalogKey()`, `layout.casRefsPrefix()`, `layout.blobsPrefix()`, and `layout.casManifestsPrefix()` after table open, with a positive namespace-file write control.; `CasPlainObjects::listNamespaceFiles` derives its LIST prefix from `layout.namespaceFilesPrefix(life)` and does not access `layout.refCatalogKey()`.; The `ListThroughHeldLifeIssuesZeroCatalogRequests` contract requires exactly one LIST of the namespace-files prefix and no other counted backend request, as enforced by `listCount(prefix) == 1`, `listTotal() == 1`, and `touchedKeys() == {prefix}`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1b-report.md#L1-L12", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1b-review.md#L30-L45", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t1c3-report.md#L5-L30", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-r1-verbatim-file-aliasing-closure.md#read-and-delayed-write-aliasing", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-stage-b-midpoint-audit.md#t6-6-namespace-file-apis-and-hot-path-catalog-gets", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-stage-b-midpoint-audit.md#t8-2-4-which-claims-might-need-a-post-task-6-correction", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3188", "topic": "read path claim", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B028-031"], "canonical_claim": "The snapshot publication unit preserves the order immutable snapshot body durable \u2192 `_ckpt` advances via `publishCkptContribution` \u2192 new snapshot adopted in memory, and the two durable effects are not separately callable.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-6b"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3189", "topic": "namespace-life capture and rebirth safety", "target": "architecture/read-path", "member_ids": ["B028-032", "B028-034", "B032-003", "B032-029"], "canonical_claim": "A reader holds a `NamespaceLifeId` handle and may return stale data or `NotFound` after removal, but must never read a newer incarnation and must not perform a hot-path fence or catalog read. Additionally, Delayed namespace-file writes capture the exact `NamespaceLifeId` at admission; a callback must not capture only `RootNamespace` and resolve the life when `finalizeImpl` runs. Additionally, A reader or `CaInlineWriteBuffer` retains the exact `NamespaceLifeId` selected at operation start and does not re-resolve the namespace name during that operation. Additionally, `CaInlineWriteBuffer` captures a `NamespaceLifeId` by value at buffer-open time and calls `putNamespaceFile(life, name, ...)` at finalization rather than capturing a bare `RootNamespace` and re-resolving it.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-r1-verbatim-file-aliasing-closure.md#read-and-delayed-write-aliasing", "docs/superpowers/cas/2026-08-02-stage-b-midpoint-audit.md#t6-5-the-delayed-cainlinewritebuffer-callback-contradicted-alre", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-6"]}

